      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T10:06:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This shader is a bit weird in how it runs validation iteratively on the dimensions. Would something like this work?\n\n```\nvar workgroups \u003d vec3u(\n    clientParams.data[uniformParams.clientOffsetInU32 + 0],\n    clientParams.data[uniformParams.clientOffsetInU32 + 1],\n    clientParams.data[uniformParams.clientOffsetInU32 + 2],\n);\n\nbool valid \u003d true;\n\n// Check that no dimension exceeds maxComputeWorkgroupsPerDimension\nif (max(max(workgroups.x, workgroups.y), workgroups.z) \u003e uniformParams.maxComputeWorkgroupsPerDimension) {\n    valid \u003d false;\n}\n\n// Check that the total number of workgroups doesn\u0027t exceed the maximum.\nif (maxWorkgroupsAllowed \u003e 0) {\n    var totalWorkgroupXY \u003d workgroups.x * workgroups.y;\n    var totalWorkgroupXYZ \u003d totalWorkgroupXY * workgroups.z;\n    \n    // Check for overflow, or one dimesion being 0.\n    if (min(totalWorkgroupXY, totalWorkgroupXYZ) \u003c workgroups.x) {\n        valid \u003d false;\n    }\n}\n\nif (validationEnabled \u0026\u0026 !valid) {\n    workgroups \u003d vec3(0);\n}\n\n// write out and duplicate if needed.\n```\n\nIt\u0027s more code but much less \"smart\".",
      "revId": "69c01ccfae899115bae75779c27aa2a646778fe1",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
