      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T10:06:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of setters called in various places, can we add `MaybeError InitializeImpl() final` here that\n\n1) get `mUsesLinearIndex` and `mUsesGlobalInvocationIndex` from the ShaderModule metadata directly in `ComputePipeline` instead of [2] so that logic is more local (also no need to skip if validation is not enabled, since getting the info is super cheap and in cold code)\n2) calls a new `virtual ResultOrError\u003cExtent3D\u003e InitializeComputeImpl()` that\u0027s implemented in all backends and returns the actual workgroup size?\n\nThis way we are guaranteed that if initialization passes, the workgroup size is set, so the member can be an `Extent3D` instead of `optional\u003cvector\u003e`.",
